<div class="section green-knit-bg" data-anchor="android_apps">
  <div class="green-bg block apps-block">
    <%= render "up_arrow", target: "projects" %>
    <h1 class="apps-title">Android Apps</h1>
    <p class="apps-intro">
      These Kotlin apps were almost entirely written by Claude, Anthropic's AI coding assistant, with me
      in the driver's seat: deciding what each app should do and how it should feel, testing it, and
      steering every change. They've been a good excuse to learn Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, but mostly
      I wanted these apps to exist, and I wanted to see how far I could get by leveraging Claude to build them.
    </p>
    <div class="projects-container">
      <% @android_apps.each do |app| %>
        <%= render "project_card", project: app %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%= render "down_arrow", target: "credits" %>
  </div>
</div>
